{"title":"1996 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1996 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We are given a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and a rectangular board <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba81326f195563e6767052c6196f3a715b3bdd95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB|=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a0b26fed2f8f16fc21e51070aa140d44e3a2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|BC|=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />.  The rectangle is divided into a grid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad074b4bc0ce2607d1255b74ecd15b336439412e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\times 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> unit squares.  The following moves are permitted on the board: one can move from one square to another only if the distance between the centers of the two squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3e9006ecc9debb184b411a0fb4e94a291b9b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. The task is to find a sequence of moves leading from the square with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as a vertex to the square with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as a vertex.\n</p><p>(a) Show that the task cannot be done if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(b) Prove that the task is possible when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40d2b05bd519f5b621323d3e471e7e0d2dc2d0d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(c) Can the task be done when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fddf04433ddeed9e04e60e99127f57505393eea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=97$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point inside triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678806ad5d445baca33dbd41186586309c37beed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle APB-\\angle ACB = \\angle APC-\\angle ABC\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the incenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b38136cabb69ee2f7b5711190e0042354f3419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d91d2a29d7b4556be19a003b0f830b700cdf92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, respectively.  Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meet at a point.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of nonnegative integers.  Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to itself such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1c7297b8725e7d5c85d5067c624a51fdc4180c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m+f(n))=f(f(m))+f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" />      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c71f46dff316c0aba06a7ae1875ca056247a8551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall m,n \\in S.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are such that the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c80d70559199764894020197142b988b09399a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15a+16b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9adba25b3d09e8d488bb9fe6bfecb5032d77f7a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16a-15b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> are both squares of positive integers.  What is the least possible value that can be taken on by the smaller of these two squares?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> be a convex hexagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193c5caa0ee1174e95025208873f5495493a2059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f55c9533d85621686c8feac06741dea37739ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba8ff65e7bed00b57423f451334d0718fe8fa94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab130b554aba74514720c42e5363c228ec33118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> denote the circumradii of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b66ed8804598d6133c4f90f551e73be8b215f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FAB$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the perimeter of the hexagon.  Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e793536b999b6ec6a59f6eef5adfcf65f0cf2d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{A}+R_{C}+R_{E} \\ge \\frac{P}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f9543229ecb2ffcede3775f96f9de55b5492bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> be three positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa0677036e16363fd2e002f0e0e134d0e710885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d67607afc34735a1289450b7c2ffdad651caaee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> be an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />-tuple of integers satisfying the following conditions:\n</p><p>(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/9846f57158e39bc4c966266b0cd5eac309dda3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=x_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />;\n</p><p>(ii) For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df494c8387fa66128e66d85a679159b8475a1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i-x_{i-1}=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d56c1424220c74e7b0c8a25cd3d3a91922bf8d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i-x_{i-1}=-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Show that there exists indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e48178aa489d4b0f872c6a72fa77d56fc64e28c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j) \\ne (0,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f31223ddc05eafff86941df2691c6b6eea849f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO\" title=\"1996 IMO\">1996 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO\" title=\"1996 IMO\">1996 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO\" title=\"1995 IMO\">1995 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"